---
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
---

<Site
  title="About"
  current="about"
  description="The Doorman Fallacy explains Rory Sutherland's idea and keeps a sourced ledger of what happened after organisations cut roles for AI."
>
  <div class="page">
    <PageHead
      title="About"
      lead="The Doorman Fallacy explains one idea, and keeps a record of what happens when organisations overlook it."
    />

    <section class="about section grid" aria-label="About the site">
      <div class="about__body stack">
        <p>
          The site has two parts. <a href="/idea">The idea</a> explains Rory Sutherland&rsquo;s doorman fallacy:
          judging a job by its most visible task, and replacing the task. <a href="/ledger">The ledger</a> follows
          organisations that cut roles because AI was to do the work, and checks back on each one over time.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is independent, with no advertising and no sponsors. How the cases are found, written and checked is
          set out in <a href="/approach">How the ledger is kept</a>.
        </p>
        <p>Write to <a href="mailto:hello@thedoormanfallacy.com">hello@thedoormanfallacy.com</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Site>

<style>
  .about {
    border-block-end: 0;
  }

  .about__body {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    max-inline-size: var(--measure);
  }
</style>
